the Lego Batman movie was a ton of fun  and had loads of cool moments in it lots  of which I've talked about in my Easter  eggs video but what I want to talk about  here is the stuff that didn't make it  into the final film  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  and in this video I'm going to break  down some of the fascinating deleted  scenes and rejected concepts from the  movie I'm also giving away a second set  of awesome Lego Batman movie books that  is the essential guide plus the making  of the movie which features concept art  sketches and Lego builds for a chance to  win make sure you subscribe and leave a  comment on this video about your  favorite deleted scene or what you'd  like to see in a sequel and for bonus  ways to enter the giveaway check out the  gleam link in the video description  below  quick alert there are spoilers ahead so  to avoid those grab the nearest bat  train out of here by clicking or tapping  the screen for my spoiler free review of  the film Lego Batman director Chris  McKay says that the idea for the Phantom  Zone housing various villains and the  wider Lego universe was inspired by  movies like cabin in the woods and Last  Action Hero  McKay wanted to bring in a bunch of  crazy villains that didn't exist in the  Batman or DC Comics universe and mix  them up with a bunch of Batman  characters and we do get a number of  uber villains such as Voldemort our Ron  and the Daleks in the movie but there  were also some r-rated villains that  McKay wanted to include in the film but  he had to leave them out as they weren't  appropriate for a younger audience  dropped from the final film was bill  from Quentin Tarantino's Kill Bill  Stephen King's Annie from the 1990  horror movie misery and bill the butcher  from Gangs of New York apparently housed  in 2001 a Space Odyssey was also removed  as a character didn't read well in the  movie although Barbara Gordon has a  backstory in the movie which differs  quite considerably from her various  comic book incarnations early versions  of the character were initially also  quite different to what's in the final  film originally barbara was known to be  a librarian at the Gotham City Library  and was secretly involved in outside the  law vigilante activities in one early  design her vigilante persona carries a  copy of The Scarlet Pimpernel who is a  character created in the last century  who also held a secret hero identity or  was a literary forerunner of characters  like Batman before deciding on a more  classic design for Robin some zany  options were considered including  Robin Hood inspired costume a  contemporary hoodie and a gymnast outfit  there was also a storyboard scene that  was cut which featured an open day at  dick Grayson's orphanage where he tried  to get attention from prospective  parents who might adopt him and as a  reference to this in the final movie  when Dick Grayson asked Bruce Wayne for  advice on how to improve his adoption  chances we get to see the Joker cruising  around in his notorious lowrider during  the movie but the lego design team  considered numerous other rides for the  Clown Prince of Crime and his sidekick  villains including an octopus and slide  vehicle that looked really cool there  were also some other Joker truck designs  that incorporated some of his classic  weapons such as a handshake joy buzzer  which electrocutes its victims and the  squirting flower that the Joker has  often worn on his jacket and which  spewed toxic gas or acid at its victims  The Joker's partner-in-crime Harley  Quinn has a rich history in the DC  Universe and numerous possible costume  designs were considered before the  filmmakers decided on her character's  final looks in the movie we also briefly  see her alter ego psychiatrist dr.  Harleen Quinzel alternative versions of  Quinzel were also considered but didn't  make it to the final film for example a  holistic therapist who provided massages  acupuncture and other treatments to  clients such as Batman  the two-face we see in the movie is the  LEGO version of what director Chris  McKay thought Billy Dee Williams as  two-face would have looked like if he  had a chance to appear on screen I shall  no doubt remember Billy Dee Williams  played Harvey Dent in Tim Burton's 1989  Batman movie but the character was  dropped from the sequel Batman Returns  alternate designs the two-face were  considered for the Lego Batman movie  though each of which paid homage to the  various incarnations the character has  appeared in the comics and on the big  and small screen over the years the  joseph's henchmen each have their own  rides and many of them also had some  very cool designs that were rejected for  the final movie The Riddler had designed  for a question mark shaped helicopter  and a double-decker berth but those were  dropped and instead he got his own  sports car there also various feline  inside vehicles considered a Catwoman  before the filmmakers settled on a  motorcycle and various wacky flying  contraptions were designed for scarecrow  before he ended up with a much simpler  flying broomstick inspired helicopter  there are also a few scenes from the  trailers it didn't  it into the final movie such as a  deleted gag where Bruce Wayne is  beatboxing and then tells Alfred's that  he should always be recording and then  we've seen a Batman running with the  other Justice League members in the  background  hence the deleted action scene with  Batman and the rest of the Justice  League  shipping Batgirl and Batman has been a  controversial subject among comic book  fans that resurfaced in last year's  animated Killing Joke movie which  included a now infamous sex scene  between the two characters marketing for  the Lego Batman movie seemed to play up  the possibility of a romantic  relationship between Batgirl and Batman  and there was a scene in a TV spot where  Barbara Gordon comments that it's been a  great first day and Batman thinks she  said first date in the final movie this  joke was cut out perhaps to the relief  of many fans of course the film still  played around with Batman having a crush  on Barbara however it doesn't lead  anywhere  and Batman jokes at the end that she's  his platonic coworker buddy who's a girl  but just a friend one of the best scenes  from the movie that we did see is where  Batman sings who's the Batman and  important to the story were other  musical themes like Michael Jackson's  man in the mirror and the final song  friends a family but director Chris  McKay is said that ideally he wanted to  make the whole movie a musical with  additional songs from different  characters perspectives integrated  throughout the film in the end the idea  of including additional musical numbers  was dropped as there wasn't enough time  to work these into the movie so guys  what do you think about the deleted  scenes villains and designs are there  any you would like to have seen in the  final movie and what would you like to  see happen in a Lego Batman sequel don't  forget to leave a comment and subscribe  for a chance to win this awesome pair of  Lego Batman movie books the bonus ways  to enter the giveaway check out the  gleam link in the video description  below if you enjoyed this do please hit  that like button and remember to turn on  your notifications for flicks in the  city so you can catch my new videos and  if you fancy finding out more about the  Lego Batman movie or other movie deleted  scenes you can tap or click here to do  just that thanks for watching and see  you next time you be going we be lovers
 

